# RecipeArchive Flutter App Environment Configuration
# This file shows the required environment variables for the Flutter app
#
# IMPORTANT: The Flutter app references the main project .env file at ../.env
# This example file is for documentation purposes only
#
# To set up the environment:
# 1. Copy the main project's .env.example to .env in the project root
# 2. Fill in the values as documented in the main .env.example
#
# The following variables are required by the Flutter app:

# API Gateway URL for backend communication
API_GATEWAY_URL=https://your-api-gateway.execute-api.region.amazonaws.com/prod

# AWS Cognito configuration for authentication
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=region_XXXXXXXXX
COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID=your-cognito-app-client-id

# Web application URL for CORS and redirects
WEB_APP_URL=https://your-cloudfront-distribution.cloudfront.net

# NOTE: These values should match the ones in the main project's .env file
# The Flutter app loads environment variables from ../.env at build time